<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harmonia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harmonia was a goddess of Greek myth, the daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ares">Ares</a> and Aphrodite and the wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cadmus">Cadmus</a>, founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a>. The gods attended their wedding, at which she received a necklace that brought misfortune to all who later owned it. In some traditions she and Cadmus ended their lives ruling the Illyrian Enchelei before being changed into serpents.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harmonia.jpg" alt="Harmonia" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Allen Shue · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_Harmonia_old_economy_village_pa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
